<mxfile host="Electron">
  <diagram name="Page-1" id="_U1EXsD85sSZjEtRVP2c">
    <mxGraphModel dx="2265" dy="3207" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1300" pageHeight="1800" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Java 7 (and earlier)&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="160" x="105" y="15" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-3" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;In Java 7, an &lt;strong style=&quot;&quot;&gt;interface was considered as &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;pure abstraction&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;which was&lt;strong style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;designed only to represent a &lt;strong style=&quot;&quot;&gt;contract&lt;/strong&gt;. It could contain &lt;strong style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;only abstract methods&lt;/strong&gt;, i.e., methods without implementation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Any &lt;strong&gt;concrete class&lt;/strong&gt; implementing that interface &lt;strong style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;must provide implementation for every abstract method&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;If a class doesn&#39;t provide implementation for all the abstract methods, it &lt;strong style=&quot;&quot;&gt;must be declared as an &lt;code&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;abstract&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/code&gt; class&lt;/strong&gt;. Such an abstract class can leave the remaining methods unimplemented, but &lt;strong style=&quot;&quot;&gt;eventually, the first concrete subclass must implement all of them&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="175" width="820" x="410" y="-40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-5" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Java 8&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Default Method + &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Static Method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="310" x="86" y="382.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-6" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp; Default Method (&lt;code style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;default&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/code&gt; keyword)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Java 8 introduced the &lt;code style=&quot;font-weight: bold; background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;default&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;b&gt; keyword &lt;/b&gt;which&amp;nbsp;allowed an interface to contain methods with implementation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;An implementing class &lt;strong&gt;is not required&lt;/strong&gt; to override a default method. It can either use the default implementation provided by the interface or override it with its own implementation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;The main purpose of introducing default methods was &lt;strong style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;backward compatibility&lt;/strong&gt;. Earlier, adding a new abstract method to an existing interface forced every implementing class to implement it, otherwise the code would not compile.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;With default methods, a new method can be added to an existing interface &lt;strong&gt;without breaking existing implementations&lt;/strong&gt;, because the interface itself provides a default implementation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;u style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 15px; white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Note&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;A default method is &lt;strong&gt;optional for the implementing class&lt;/strong&gt;, not for the interface. The method already exists in the interface with its &lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;implementation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="377" width="820" x="412" y="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-8" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp; Static Method (&lt;code&gt;static&lt;/code&gt; keyword)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Before Java 8, common helper logic was usually placed in a separate &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;utility class&lt;/span&gt; (e.g., &lt;code&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;PaymentUtil&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;MathUtil&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;ValidationUtil&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/code&gt;). &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;with Java 8, such &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;utility methods replaced with static method&lt;/span&gt; which is written inside interface itself.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;A static method belongs to the &lt;strong&gt;interface itself&lt;/strong&gt;, not to its implementing classes.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;It must be called using the &lt;strong&gt;interface name&lt;/strong&gt;, i.e., &lt;code&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;InterfaceName.methodName()&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Static methods are &lt;strong&gt;not inherited&lt;/strong&gt; by implementing classes, so they &lt;strong&gt;cannot be overridden&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;Limitations in Java 8:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;If multiple static methods inside the same interface need the same common logic (e.g., &lt;i&gt;validation&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;logging&lt;/i&gt;, or &lt;i&gt;database connection setup&lt;/i&gt;), that logic has to be duplicated because Java 8 doesn&#39;t allow private methods inside interfaces.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="372" width="820" x="412" y="618" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-9" parent="1" style="ellipse;html=1;shape=endState;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="60" x="12" y="1150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-10" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Java 9&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Private Method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="80" width="155" x="88" y="1140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="axAjCV-cUVfPQJtzLNJt-1" edge="1" parent="1" source="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-11" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-10">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-11" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Java 9 introduced &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;private methods&lt;/span&gt; inside interface which can be of two types: &lt;strong style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;private instance methods&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;Private static method&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;A private method can be called &lt;strong&gt;only from within the same interface&lt;/strong&gt;. if it is a private instance method then it can be called only from default methods whereas a private static method can be called from both - &lt;strong&gt;default methods and static methods&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;The main purpose of a private method is to &lt;strong style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 222, 89), rgb(255, 222, 89));&quot;&gt;extract common logic shared by multiple default methods&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;multiple static methods&lt;/strong&gt; which helps in removing code duplication and improve maintainability.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="196" width="820" x="410" y="1081" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-18" parent="1" style="ellipse;html=1;shape=endState;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="60" x="6" y="382.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zcFhryvo-dmRWoC-DznP-19" parent="1" style="ellipse;html=1;shape=endState;fillColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;fontFamily=Georgia;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="60" x="10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
